<!--
  sensors.xml  -  PHD2 image-sensor database
  ===========================================
  Curated catalog of CMOS / CCD image sensors found in cameras commonly
  used for guiding and EAA. Used to:

    * Look up pixel size when the camera backend can't report it
      (typical for UVC / V4L2 cameras).
    * Drive smarter defaults for the noise-reduction pipeline (full-well
      / read-noise / native bit depth inform outlier thresholds).
    * Let the user explicitly select the sensor in a camera that the
      backend doesn't auto-identify.

  The selection is stored per-camera (keyed by hardware id when one is
  available, else by guide profile). Cameras that already report sensor
  info via SDK still trump anything here.

  Schema (all fields optional except <name>):
    name           : Canonical sensor part number / family name (key)
    manufacturer   : "Sony", "OmniVision", "Aptina", "ON Semi", ...
    pixel_size_um  : Pixel pitch in micrometers (square pixels assumed)
    pixel_array_w  : Active array width in pixels
    pixel_array_h  : Active array height in pixels
    bit_depth      : Native ADC depth (8 / 10 / 12 / 14 / 16)
    color_array    : "mono", "RGGB", "BGGR", "GBRG", "GRBG"
    full_well_e    : Typical saturation in electrons at unity gain
    read_noise_e   : Typical read noise in electrons at HCG / high gain
    notes          : Free-form, e.g. "back-illuminated, STARVIS"

  To add a sensor: send a PR with sourced datasheet values. Where
  vendor numbers vary by mode, prefer typical "high conversion gain"
  values - that's what most modern UVC cams expose.
-->
